    <bpmn:process id="W_W1981" name="W1981. Subscription Product Launch &amp; Go-to-Market" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Pilot evaluation approved per W1980
Frequency: Per product launch (~2–4/year)
Volume: Target: 5,000–10,000 subscribers in Year 1
Owner: CMO
Participants: CMO, VP Store Operations, Sales Associates, CFO
Source: workflow W1981 — Subscription Product Launch &amp; Go-to-Market</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1981_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1981_Lane1" name="CMO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1981_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1981_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1981_Lane2" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1981_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1981_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1981_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1981_Start4" name="Pilot evaluation approved per W1980">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1981_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1981_Task5" name="CMO develops go-to-market plan: (a) target audience: new homeowners, existing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: CMO develops go-to-market plan: (a) target audience: new homeowners, existing loyalty members who purchased eligible products, (b) channels: in-store (POS enrollment), online (website + app), email campaign to loyalty members, social media, (c) launch promotion: first-100-subscribers bonus loyalty points, (d) sales target: 5,000 subscribers in Year 1
Responsible (R): CMO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1981_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1981_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1981_Task6" name="Store-level launch: (a) train all 200 store Sales Associates on subscription…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Store-level launch: (a) train all 200 store Sales Associates on subscription selling, (b) in-store POS materials: subscription service brochures at checkout and eligible product sections, (c) Store Manager enrollment target: 8–15 subscribers/store/month for the first 3 months (≈5,000–9,000 in Q1, within the Year-1 5,000–10,000 target), (d) track enrollment by store per W35
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 week rollout</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1981_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1981_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1981_Task7" name="Post-launch monitoring: (a) weekly enrollment dashboard by store and channel…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Post-launch monitoring: (a) weekly enrollment dashboard by store and channel, (b) service completion tracking: are visits being scheduled and completed on time?, (c) customer feedback after first visit: target CSAT ≥ 4.0/5.0, (d) adjust: pricing, partner capacity, territory coverage based on initial results
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations / CMO
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1981_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1981_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1981_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1981_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1981_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-382 (ensure controlled execution — Subscription Product Design &amp; Setup (PA-47.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: CMO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
